From 3a986080e196c5d26376a8cf4c0566dc26504ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 10:40:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.0.1: fix Samba 4 file server (never started -- 3
 packaging/config gaps)

The Samba 4.15.13 integration shipped a non-functional SMB server in v2.0.0:
smbd exited on every boot, so nothing listened on 445 and Windows reported
"can't find path" / 0x80004005 in every share mode. Three independent defects,
all found on-metal (RT-BE96U, v2.0.0):

1. Loader path: smbd/nmbd/smbpasswd carry NO RUNPATH and their ~120 private
   *-samba4.so libraries install to /usr/lib/samba, which is not on the default
   search path -> "error while loading shared libraries: libcmdline-samba4.so".
   Fix: add /usr/lib/samba to rom /etc/ld.so.conf; the boot-time ldconfig
   (init.c) then registers it for every Samba binary (no RUNPATH edit, no
   LD_LIBRARY_PATH leak into pid 1).

2. Runtime dirs: start_samba() (written for Samba 3.6) only created
   /var/run/samba. Samba 4 also needs /var/lib/samba/private (msg.sock, secrets)
   and /var/log/samba, or nmbd/smbd abort at "Failed to init messaging context".
   Fix: create /var/log/samba, /var/lib/samba{,/private}, /var/cache/samba for
   the SAMBA4 path before launching.

3. Guest auth: the guest branch emitted "map to guest = Bad Password", which
   only maps a KNOWN user with a bad password -> an anonymous/unknown user is
   rejected, never mapped to guest. Fix: "map to guest = Bad User" (Samba 4
   correct; matches the anonymous-guest intent). NB: modern Windows also blocks
   insecure guest by default -- account mode is the robust client path.

Not fatal, left as-is: the config still emits Samba-3-era "auth methods" /
"use spnego" (ignored with a warning) and, when smbd_protocol=3, forces SMB3
encryption (fine for account mode, incompatible with anonymous guest).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c | 2 +-
 release/src/router/rc/usb.c                 | 9 +++++++++
 release/src/router/rom/rom/etc/ld.so.conf   | 1 +
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c b/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
index 107cda39dd..0b2941ad25 100644
--- a/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
+++ b/release/src/router/libdisk/write_smb_conf.c
@@ -423,7 +423,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 #if defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA36X) || defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA4)
 		fprintf(fp, "auth methods = guest\n");
 		fprintf(fp, "guest account = %s\n", nvram_get("http_username")? : "admin");
-		fprintf(fp, "map to guest = Bad Password\n");
+		fprintf(fp, "map to guest = Bad User\n");
 		fprintf(fp, "guest ok = yes\n");
 #else
 		fprintf(fp, "security = SHARE\n");
diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
index 8f67db33e8..415a2a3425 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
@@ -3687,6 +3687,15 @@ start_samba(void)
 	system("tsmb-server -c /etc/smb.conf -B");
 #elif defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA36X) || defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA4)
 	mkdir_if_none("/var/run/samba");
+#if defined(RTCONFIG_SAMBA4)
+	/* reaper: Samba 4 also needs these runtime dirs (private holds msg.sock/secrets,
+	   plus log/cache); the stock Samba-3.6-era path only made /var/run/samba, so without
+	   them nmbd/smbd abort at "Failed to init messaging context". */
+	mkdir_if_none("/var/log/samba");
+	mkdir_if_none("/var/lib/samba");
+	mkdir_if_none("/var/lib/samba/private");
+	mkdir_if_none("/var/cache/samba");
+#endif
 
 	xstart("/usr/sbin/nmbd", "-D", "-s", "/etc/smb.conf");
 	snprintf(smbd_cmd, sizeof(smbd_cmd), "%s/smbd", "/usr/sbin");
diff --git a/release/src/router/rom/rom/etc/ld.so.conf b/release/src/router/rom/rom/etc/ld.so.conf
index eadd23a49b..74409875fb 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rom/rom/etc/ld.so.conf
+++ b/release/src/router/rom/rom/etc/ld.so.conf
@@ -2,3 +2,4 @@
 /opt/usr/lib
 /lib
 /usr/lib
+/usr/lib/samba
-- 
2.25.1

